From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] winegstreamer: WMA decoder IMediaObject gaps, IPropertyBag / IPropertyStore, MFT input types, current types, status and messages

The WMA decoder already had the type calls of IMediaObject; the rest was
stubbed:

- IMediaObject: GetStreamCount (E_POINTER), stream info, GetInputSizeInfo
  (the input block alignment, needs an input type), max latency, Lock,
  streaming resources, GetInputStatus, Discontinuity (drains), Flush,
  ProcessInput, ProcessOutput (S_FALSE when no output, status 0, a NULL
  buffer with DISCARD_WHEN_NO_BUFFER) via dmo_transform.c.
  SetInputType with the type already set changes nothing; another type
  drops the output type (it depends on the input type).
- IMFTransform: GetInputAvailableType (the 4 WMA subtypes), Get{Input,Output}
  CurrentType, GetInputStatus, DRAIN / FLUSH / notification messages,
  ProcessEvent and GetOutputStatus (documented E_NOTIMPL, no FIXME).
- IPropertyBag keeps what is written; the object now offers IPropertyStore,
  as the conformance test expects.
- SetOutputType set the bit depth in the input type's WAVEFORMATEX instead of
  the output's.

mf transform.c: the todo_wine marks of the WMA decoder's property store,
input types and current types are removed, as is the one on
GetOutputCurrentType after a new input type.

